    18	## Camera
    19	
    20	The stage `fov` is the horizontal angle. Blender now uses
    21	`sensor_fit: HORIZONTAL` and computes `lens` from `sensor_width`, so the final
    22	track matches the stage renderer's horizontal field of view. The camera matrix
    23	is unchanged.
    24	
    25	## Overrides
    26	
    27	The white environment uses pure white color and Strength `1.0` under
    28	`view_transform: Standard`. Material colors with `sum(color) / 3 > 0.65` are
    29	replaced by `(0.55, 0.55, 0.55)`. The charcoal overrides for sheet-metal powder
    30	coating and `door_edge_meshes` are retained.
    31	
    32	Non-charcoal materials are forced to `metalness: 0.0` and `roughness >= 0.45`,
    33	including their roughness maps. Glass uses Transmission `0.0` and the
    34	non-charcoal gray color. Charcoal door-edge materials retain `metalness: 0.12`.
